revenue; and (e) research activities undertaken by both UMR Research Pty Ltd and the CSIRO supports the view that the majority of Australians are of the opinion that the economic benefits of mining in Australia are not distributed fairly. (2) That the following matter be referred to the Economics References Committee for inquiry and report on the first sitting: day in March 2020: (a) arrangements used by other countries to maximise the benefit to the public of national oil and gas reserves; (b) arrangement that could be considered to maximise benefit to the public of Australia's national oil and gas resources, cognisant of: (i) sovereign risk, (ii) existing property rights, and (iii) federal and state jurisdictions; and (c) any related matters. Peter Whish-Wilson I seek leave to make a short statement. Scott Ryan Leave is granted for one minute. Peter Whish-Wilson No-one has done more than the Greens in this chamber to pursue the tax avoidance of some of the biggest polluters on this planet, who, under the petroleum resource rent tax and other meas","result":"affirmative","slug":"division-federal-senate-10402","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2019-09-19/4"}
